{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood","id":1455892,"title":"Why does Baali blood taste the same as Tremere blood?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-31T18:06:59-07:00","id":1455892,"title":"Why does Baali blood taste the same as Tremere blood?","content":"Now I know Saulot is a rumored founder of the Baali, and I know after Saulot was diablerized that probably altered the Tremere bloodline significantly, but still the Tremere started as a Tcimizce bloodline from the potion Goratrix created.<br /> <br /> So how does that equate to tremere and Baali blood tasting the same? Did salubri blood taste the same as Baali? Or are the Baali some mix of Tcimizce and Salubri blood as well?<br /> <br /> Looking for all theories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T20:15:44-07:00","id":1455894,"title":"","content":"Owing to a quirk of fate, Tremere and Baali blood both have a minty finish.<br /> <br /> Joking aside, how many vampires would taste the blood of both the Tremere and the Baali? So they could make a comparison in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T21:21:56-07:00","id":1455899,"title":"","content":"It's probably a bit reductive to say that they taste &quot;the same,&quot; but rather that they taste &quot;close enough&quot; that you need an expert to pick apart the difference. I think it's also less a question of literal &quot;taste&quot;; I think this matter tends to come up more when Thaumaturgical testing for lineage occurs. And since the Tremere are already supposed to be this weird slurry of Tzimisce and Salubri, it's probably easier for Baali to pass themselves off as some unusual off-shoot of the Tremere than it is some other unknown Clan. Especially since plenty might have access to Dark Thaumaturgy to imitate Tremere Blood Magic.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting that this is one of those &quot;kinda common OOC knowledge, but very obscure IC knowledge&quot; topics. IIRC Aisling Sturbridge offers a side-note accusing Vykos of being a liar when the theory of Tzimisce blood being using to create the Tremere comes up in BJD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T22:00:13-07:00","id":1455902,"title":"","content":"I imagine that in exchange for leading the Tremere to Saulot, the Baali arranged for many of them to join house Tremere and underwent rituals to help with the disguise. <br /> <br /> It could also be that, because Baali kinda have mirrored disciplines of the Tremere, they taste similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T00:45:08-07:00","id":1455906,"title":"","content":"There's also been hints here and there that the Baali could have been a Tzimisci bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T01:57:14-07:00","id":1455912,"title":"","content":"Yeah, one theory is that the Baali have multiple founders, so they might be descended from both Saulot and Tzimisce. <br /> <br /> If so, their slurry of Salubri/Tzimisce blood might taste a lot like the Tremere's slurry of Salubri/Tzimisce blood.<br /> <br /> It's also worth bearing in mind that at least in Revised and V20, Saulot was in the body of Tremere. Via the alchemy of Blood Sympathy (not a concrete thing in VTM, but definitely suggested in all the fluff), it's quite feasible that the Tremere have become more like Saulot.<br /> <br /> In my games, I created a series of Merits and Flaws to show the Tremere starting to degenerate as a Clan, gaining Salubri-like traits and Tzimisce-like mutations, with some of them becoming very pale and wormy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T13:53:03-07:00","id":1455951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1455912#post1455912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, one theory is that the Baali have multiple founders, .</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that theory. They are the result of multiple clans becoming infernalists. While not all infernalists become Baali, some Infernalists got a special deal back with the Devil back in the day, resulting in multiple Baali founders. I wouldn't be surprised if such deals were fairly common back when 4rth and 5th gens were neonate trash in a world where werewolves were much more common, and mages suffered far less paradox. There may be literally hundreds of Baali founders, most of which have long since been destroyed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T15:57:02-07:00","id":1455965,"title":"","content":"Another possibility is that the &quot;Tremere blood tastes like Baali blood&quot; is an in-universe bit of propaganda, spread by enemies of the Tremere to <i>literally</i> demonize them.<br /> <br /> After all, the Tremere spread vicious rumors about the Salubri being soul-stealers. Turnabout is fair play.<br /> <br /> To be fair, the Tremere ARE pretty evil, all told. They have many enemies, and not just for petty reasons. It's just that them being blood-related to the token Infernalist bloodline doesn't necessarily need to be one of them.<br /> <br /> It might be a malicious lie by one of the Tremere's enemies. Or something that a vampire who had an opportunity to drink both (or thought they had) convinced themselves was true. Like, they fed on a Tremere and a Baali (or someone they believed to be a Baali, or just a random Infernalist), and it tasted just similar enough (in the sense that any vampire's blood tastes similar to any other) that they jumped to conclusions. This accusation then gained momentum over time, while also degenerating (as rumors often do). Until &quot;Tremere blood tastes like Baali&quot; just became accepted fact (at least among the minority of Kindred who heard of it).<br /> <br /> After all, for many vampires, &quot;Infernalist&quot; and &quot;Baali&quot; are one and the same. The distinction is unknown or lost to them. Heck, maybe Tremere blood does have a whiff of the demonic, but only because it descends from Tzimisce, who have a long history of dealings with Kupala and other lesser demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 08-01-2021, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T16:50:54-07:00","id":1455971,"title":"","content":"There used to be a fact that the survivors of the Baali were impersonating Tremere as their most common cover.<br /> <br /> Which makes NO SENSE because there is literally NO other clan that would be harder to impersonate members of given that the Tremere Pyramid has a record of each and every single member of its Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T19:46:29-07:00","id":1455987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1455971#post1455971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There used to be a fact that the survivors of the Baali were impersonating Tremere as their most common cover.<br /> <br /> Which makes NO SENSE because there is literally NO other clan that would be harder to impersonate members of given that the Tremere Pyramid has a record of each and every single member of its Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, you don't impersonate a Tremere to fool another Tremere. You impersonate them to fool everyone else.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I would argue that while the Pyramid has records of every member of the Clan, every member of the Clan does not have access to those records. Not every Tremere knows every other Tremere.<br /> <br /> Especially during the medieval era, when it's difficult for any Kindred to cross the countryside. If some Kindred shows up at a chantry claiming to be a Tremere, it would take a while to verify their claim. Not to mention if a Baali caught a Tremere in transit between cities, and assumed their identity. If you've never met the real person before, would you know they weren't who they said they were? Especially if they come bearing (stolen) letters of introduction from an Elder?<br /> <br /> It's hardly fool proof, of course. But in pre-modern times, a desperate or brazen Baali might not get found out for a while, if they're found out at all. If nothing else, it seems like a ploy that would work for some time, until the Clan grew wise to the trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T02:27:29-07:00","id":1455997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1455951#post1455951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that theory. They are the result of multiple clans becoming infernalists. While not all infernalists become Baali, some Infernalists got a special deal back with the Devil back in the day, resulting in multiple Baali founders. I wouldn't be surprised if such deals were fairly common back when 4rth and 5th gens were neonate trash in a world where werewolves were much more common, and mages suffered far less paradox. There may be literally hundreds of Baali founders, most of which have long since been destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, the version of that origin story in Black Hand and other V20 books has nothing to do with the Devil or bargains. Indeed, most Baali don't really truck with anything as mundane as the Devil, but rather older, more eldritch things, which predate the Abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea is that it's the Well at Chorazin that makes Baali. So any vampire thrown into it, or Embraced within it, emerges as Baali. This is the basis of the spawning rite used, for instance, to make Apostates (those who convert to Baali from other Clans and Bloodlines).<br /> <br /> The origin myth of the three 'founders' states that Saulot (or another) punished the mortal infernalists at Chorazin by attacking them and throwing them into the Well. He then poured some of his vitae in afterwards, for reasons unknown (Transylvania Chronicles suggests Saulot wants to become the Demon Emperor, so perhaps that's why). <br /> <br /> The three who crawled through the mass of broken bodies and drank this vitae emerged as the three Baali founders, known as Moloch, Nergal and the Unnamed. <br /> <br /> Thereafter, the Baali would often make sacrificial wells that, through such grotesque acts of evil, effectively become Nihils or similar (i.e., shallow points between the Skinlands and the realms of the dreaming Neverborn, who may or may not be the same as the Children).<br /> <br /> It's very close to the idea of Nephandi being made through a caul, which I think is intentional. The story as told in more recent supplements hints that multiple Antediluvians may have come across the Well, rather than just one, meaning the founders may have been created at separate times (or perhaps multiple Antediluvians travelled together and punished the human infernalists).<br /> <br /> Now, I think you may be referring to the lore as told in Chaos Factor (now retconned), where a band of Methuselahs from the times of the Book of Nod followed Shaitan in offering themselves up as servants to a demon called Baal, thus becoming Baali. <br /> <br /> I think the V20 version of events is probably an attempt to integrate the conflicting lore somewhat (the buried and entombed bodies of the Children are implied to be physical manifestations or shells of the Neverborn, in a nod to the Qlippoth of Mage, who must be kept aslept lest their dreaming minds and entombed bodies reunite and awaken in the Skinlands). <br /> <br /> I also think it links back to the apocryphal history of ur-Shulgi which was removed from the Revised Clanbook Assamite. In that book, ur-Shulgi is hinted to be a Widderslainte, who is thrown into the Well by Haqim, emerges as some sort of Nephandi/dark blood mage, and rallies the Baali to make them easier to strike as one. The Baali are thus defeated and Haqim proceeds to tear the demon/inverted Avatar inhabiting ur-Shulgi's body and Embraces him as an Assamite. In this way, Haqim might be a third Baali progenitor.<br /> <br /> The complicating factor (and these always exist in the WoD) is that Lore of the Bloodlines represents yet another story, where the Children are the First People, which potentially makes them Fallen rather than manifestations of the Neverborn. But it might also be true that the Neverborn are just the souls of a primordial race who strode the cosmos before the VTM Yahweh decimated/usurped them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-02-2021, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T11:07:57-07:00","id":1456018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1455997#post1455997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the idea is that it's the Well at Chorazin that makes Baali. So any vampire thrown into it, or Embraced within it, emerges as Baali. This is the basis of the spawning rite used, for instance, to make Apostates (those who convert to Baali from other Clans and Bloodlines).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think originally the idea was just that &quot;they're both bloodlines of the Salubri!&quot; (cue ominous music), your post made me think there may be an additional reason IC.<br /> <br /> Both the original Tremere self-vampirization ritual, and this strange Baali ritual might have similar affects on their blood indicating that it is some kind of &quot;tampering&quot; with the blood that resulted in something not &quot;normal&quot; for vitae. Some kind of &quot;contamination&quot; entered the vitae as a result of the rituals, and it is this that is being tasted. It's like how anyone who brews their own beer or makes their own wine can immediately tell when something went wrong (usually as a result of not sanitizing the lines properly) because certain mistakes result in a very recognizable taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-03-2021, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T08:06:41-07:00","id":1456072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1456018#post1456018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the idea is that it's the Well at Chorazin that makes Baali. So any vampire thrown into it, or Embraced within it, emerges as Baali. This is the basis of the spawning rite used, for instance, to make Apostates (those who convert to Baali from other Clans and Bloodlines)./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> While I think originally the idea was just that &quot;they're both bloodlines of the Salubri!&quot; (cue ominous music), your post made me think there may be an additional reason IC. <br /> <br /> Both the original Tremere self-vampirization ritual, and this strange Baali ritual might have similar affects on their blood indicating that it is some kind of &quot;tampering&quot; with the blood that resulted in something not &quot;normal&quot; for vitae. Some kind of &quot;contamination&quot; entered the vitae as a result of the rituals, and it is this that is being tasted. It's like how anyone who brews their own beer or makes their own wine can immediately tell when something went wrong (usually as a result of not sanitizing the lines properly) because certain mistakes result in a very recognizable taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really interesting. I love that. In some cases, then, it might be a threefold similarity: Saulot's blood, Tzimisce's blood and the taste of 'counterfeit' vitae. (And maybe it's four points of similarity if blood magic itself changes the taste.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T12:41:22-07:00","id":1456255,"title":"","content":"I might be out of the loop here but.... where is it stated that Tremere blood &quot;tastes&quot; like anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T13:43:52-07:00","id":1456262,"title":"","content":"I imagine if you ask a Tremere their blood tastes like power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T14:41:44-07:00","id":1456264,"title":"","content":"If it's V20 Tremere, their answer would probably be, &quot;I wouldn't know, I don't drink other Kindred's blood. Do I look insane?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 08-06-2021, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T23:49:05-07:00","id":1456281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1456255#post1456255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be out of the loop here but.... where is it stated that Tremere blood &amp;quot;tastes&amp;quot; like anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember, but I know it's mentioned in the books. Maybe it was Transylvanian Chronicles or something like that? Or Lore of the Bloodlines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T01:46:53-07:00","id":1456288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1456262#post1456262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine if you ask a Tremere their blood tastes like power.</div> </div> </div> </div>/Assamite sorcerers literally believe their weakness (prominent aura, screws with obfuscate) is because they're too fucking powerful. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T13:13:21-07:00","id":1456311,"title":"","content":"While not canon, a good-enough-for-homebrew answer could be that the Tremere really used Baali vitae to turn themselves, and allowed other Cainites to assume they had experimented on their fellow Transylvanians because it was less scandalous than being known as a Baali bloodline. This would all be a major secret, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T23:50:33-07:00","id":1456336,"title":"","content":"I think everyone gave a good summary<br /> <br /> 1) At first the Tremere were created through magic, and many Baali are created through the rite of apostacy, that while is a Dark Thaumaturgy ritual, is still magical. Even more the current origin of the Baali (V20) is focused on a unnatural creation via the Well of Ashur, making the Baali some sort of &quot;artificial&quot; bloodline, quite like the Tremere.<br /> <br /> 2) In their first days the Tremere were a bloodline of Carpathian Tzimisce. More specifically they used the blood of Roland, childe of Rustovich, childe of Kosczecsyku, childe of Yorak, making them descendents of Yorak. The Tzimisces are often hinted as one of the origins of the Baali (Tzimisce Revised, Black Hand revised), and among them Yorak is deeply suspicious : he was probably the wickedest of the children of the Eldest and, even more important, he lived in a underground place made of flesh and bones (anyone said Tophet?), frolicking with one of the mightiest demon the World of Darkness ever knew while becoming the most accomplished Koldun (magic that bounds demons and evil natural spirits) on Earth.<br /> <br /> While it's almost sure that Ur-Shulgi is the Unnamed, among the traits of the Unnamed there were these<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Others claim it was in fact a pair of lovers merged together at the organ pit, thus explaining the presence of hermaphroditic deities in various ancient societies. Yet others claim it was a beautiful </span></span></span><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Slave_Boy\" target=\"_blank\">slave boy</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> rescued by the Cainite and brought back to the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Second_City\" target=\"_blank\">Second City</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The most popular theory is that the third Baali is female.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Which would fit quite well with Yorak, since he is a confirmed hermaphroditic and at the time of his (her?) embrace he was a woman. As far as I remember Yorak is the only &quot;hermaphroditic&quot; 4th gen of the lore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3) All the Tremere higher-ups diablerized the higher ups of the Salubri clan, and Tremere himself drank Saulot, sharing his body with him after that. To the current day the Tremere are more salubri than anything else. This is somewhat hinted also in V5, where out of 3 disciplines Salubri and Tremere share 2 (Auspex and Dominate). We know for a fact that at least one of the Baali (Nergal for sure, but Moloch too probably) is a direct children of Saulot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-08-2021, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T17:26:06-07:00","id":1456476,"title":"","content":"Don't the Baali have some sort of ritual to 'convert' recruits from other clans into Baali? In which case the ritual likely messes around with the Cainite curse in such a way it might also alter how Baali Vitae is 'perceived' by others. Without knowing what the exact differences entail though, how this is interpreted is probably up for debate (is it similar because they had atypical origins compared to 'traditional' vampires, or is it a result of magical meddling, or is it just because the Baali had some Tremere recruits and someone just managed to get ahold of some to 'taste'?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T00:17:44-07:00","id":1456502,"title":"","content":"I can't recall if the Baali apostasy was a longstanding ritual or something thrown in with the experiment that was DAV20, but I don't really like the idea that Baali could be the vampire equivalent to BSDs or Nephandi, and that you can refuse to be embraced by them because true damnation requires consent. They work best as regular vampires that are too close to the devil, not as some innately double-damned bloodline of cartoonish evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T01:24:52-07:00","id":1456507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1456502#post1456502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't recall if the Baali apostasy was a longstanding ritual or something thrown in with the experiment that was DAV20, but I don't really like the idea that Baali could be the vampire equivalent to BSDs or Nephandi, and that you can refuse to be embraced by them because true damnation requires consent. They work best as regular vampires that are too close to the devil, not as some innately double-damned bloodline of cartoonish evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's there in Clanbook: Baali from the original VTDA line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T06:58:29-07:00","id":1456529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1456507#post1456507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's there in Clanbook: Baali from the original VTDA line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I want to say there's <i>something</i> about it in <i>House of Tremere</i> as well. That's the one splatbook that goes into detail about the practice of infernalism within the clan, the various secret societies within it, and...maybe?...Baali within the clan who are either apostates or &quot;pure&quot; Baali, whose clanhood is more of an open secret than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T13:24:10-07:00","id":1456694,"title":"","content":"I believe House of Tremere mention Etrius dabbling in infernalism in an attempt to figure out an alternative to the decline of magick but that may have occured either before Goratrix stumbled on his 'solution' to the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T11:58:55-07:00","id":1456822,"title":"","content":"For those wondering why Tremere care about the &quot;taste&quot; or &quot;character&quot; of blood, remember that one of their big bargaining chips in Vampiric society is their ability to confirm generation, past diablerie, clan, bloodline, vampiric heraldry. A Tremere isn't &quot;drinking&quot; vitae on the regular, but a touch, sniff or lick is enough to get a sense of what's going on.<br /> <br /> As a result, it is very important that Baali blood &quot;tastes&quot; (not always literally with the tongue) similar enough to Tremere. A sharp Tremere, or a paranoid one, might think that they were tasting the blood of an offshoot such as the Telvyanic or Antitribu, or perhaps that the blood was unusual in some way, but to most it would just be regular old Tremere blood. This is the writers adding plausibility into the existence of Baali in the Camarilla, since they have an in-built cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T00:16:16-07:00","id":1464979,"title":"","content":"To the OP Question<br /> <br /> Why would Tremere and Baali Blood taste alike?<br /> <br /> 1) They may share the same founder(s). Tremere came from Tzimisce, Saulot and Gangrel. Baali, depending on the myth you go with, also were created by Saulot, Tzimisce and / or Ennoia.<br /> 2) The Baali may have been behind the Tremeres creation and purposefully shown them a ritual that would make their blood similiar or sneak in Baali blood when they turned<br /> 3) The taste similiarity might come from thaumaturgy which both clans use and have, and ultimately stems from demons<br /> 4) it might be a &quot;mistake&quot; cause the Tremere are super infested by Baali, so the Baali tested as Tremere might actually not have been a real Tremere. Also there uis a lot of Tremere Apostates that would be listed and known as Tremere while having Baali blood (as the Re Embrace overrides your original blood thus giving you daimonion and the Baali clan weakness)<br /> 5) It may be that all vampires that were magicly created (Tremere, Baali, Nagaraja) may have a similiar taste<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1455971#post1455971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There used to be a fact that the survivors of the Baali were impersonating Tremere as their most common cover.<br /> <br /> Which makes NO SENSE because there is literally NO other clan that would be harder to impersonate members of given that the Tremere Pyramid has a record of each and every single member of its Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i strongly disagree. First, the &quot;order of the wyrm&quot; is an actual order in clan tremere that is run by an infested by Baali exclusively and the Molochim use them to recruit apostates and it is stated in multiple sources that is the go to clan for new Baali.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> 1) Baali and Tremere blood is very similiar, youd need Auspex 6 to notice a difference<br /> 2) Tremere often dabble into infernalism in their pursuit of knowledge and are more lenient with such studies than any other clan<br /> 3) Actually one of the council of 7 is a Baali (Thomas Wyncham) and he is in the inncer council, while is sire, or circumstances of embrace are unknown. Also its not like you cant fabricate a story.<br /> 4) Dark thaumaturgy is a (almost) Baali exclusive extension of regular thaumaturgy so they can easily use the Tremere signature discipline.<br /> 5) Baali are very well versed in the occult and politicing and masquerading they shuldnt have issues to fit in with the Tremere<br /> 6) The Baali may have had a guiding hand in the creation of the Tremere, giving Goratrix the idea and leading Tremere to Saulots tomb.<br /> <br /> 7) The Tremere originate in the dark ages where record keeping wasnt quite fantastic. if the Baali got into the Clan Tremere early on it wouldnt be difficult for those already inside creating cover stories and identities for new Baali.<br /> <br /> 8) Also note that Baali are, on average, super driven and highly intelligent seekers of knowledge and power with no morals holding them back. They are the perfect candidates for Clan Tremere vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 10-23-2021, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T04:42:50-07:00","id":1464998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455892-why-does-baali-blood-taste-the-same-as-tremere-blood?p=1464979#post1464979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the OP Question<br /> <br /> 3) Actually one of the council of 7 is a Baali (Thomas Wyncham) and he is in the inncer council, while is sire, or circumstances of embrace are unknown. Also its not like you cant fabricate a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>From where do you get this one? Is it his apprentice Oliver Thrace having Dark Thaumaturgy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}